  'Included for Australian healthtech, medtech and digital-health founder matching: Australian Medical Angels is an official national clinician angel syndicate founded from a 2017 origin story, with 1,000+ clinician investors, 30+ portfolio companies and A$18M deployed according to 2026 media, and it launched Medical Angels Venture Fund I as a A$40M ESVCLP in 2026. The fund page states a strategy of 30-40 portfolio companies, A$100k-A$500k initial cheques, around 50% reserved for follow-ons, and leading when its clinical edge is highest. The main stage_focus is kept to pre_seed and seed because the founder-facing flow and official initial-cheque guidance are early-stage; do not treat it as an ordinary Series A lead VC despite follow-on capacity and co-investment rights. recent_deals now include Clean Slate Clinic''s 2026 structured financing and GXE''s 2025 Series A. Clean Slate is strong healthtech / clinical evidence but is not a normal priced equity round and should not drive cheque_ranges. GXE is valid in-window participation evidence but is a fund administration / private-assets SaaS company, so it should not strengthen the healthtech thesis. Telecare remains lead-capable historical evidence only until a dated financing close is found. lead_behavior is lead-capable in healthtech / clinical-edge rounds, not evidence that every recent round is led by Medical Angels. screening_priority is high for healthtech-specific matching.'
