  'Included for ANZ early-stage VC matching: TEN13 is a network-driven, syndicated VC rather than a passive platform, with official first-cheque guidance of US$300k-US$2m across pre-seed, seed and beyond, 500+ network investors, and a 2025 QIC Queensland Venture Capital Development Fund mandate. Core first-cheque matching should prioritise pre_seed and seed; series_a is supported by official flexibility and recent participation but should be lower weight than early-stage matching. lead_behavior = co_lead because TEN13 led Flyweel''s 2026 A$2.4m pre-seed round and co-led OneMRI''s seed round, while other in-window deals show participant behaviour. geography_focus includes global because official pages say TEN13 backs global ambition and recent deals include US and UK companies, but ANZ remains the strongest founder-matching geography because TEN13 positions itself as an Australia & New Zealand syndicated venture platform. recent_deals are sourced mainly from TEN13 official deal memos; external verification was found for OneMRI via media coverage, while Flyweel/Appetise/Atrium/MiLaboratories/Streamkap should be treated as official-source supported pending independent round verification. Do not treat TEN13 like Aussie Angels: it has platform/syndication mechanics, but it also acts as investor and VC manager.'
