  'medium',
  'Included for ANZ pre-seed and seed angel-syndicate routing, not for recent-deal-similarity scoring: CMACK Ventures is Cheryl Mack''s Aussie Angels-hosted syndicate. The official page says Cheryl is Aussie Angels CEO / co-founder, Black Nova Venture Partner, 361 Angel Club co-founder, has been angel investing for nearly six years with 32 portfolio companies and 8 fund investments, and leads CMACK Ventures with nearly 500 investors writing cheques into seed startups. The stated thesis is B2B companies with A+ founders, painful problems, huge market opportunity and a clear way Cheryl can help, especially marketing, GTM, branding, content, storytelling, B2B sales funnels, startup/customer access and VC-backed fundraising pathways. Interpret enterprise as B2B software / workflow / scalable SaaS, not long enterprise procurement cycles; the official page explicitly says founders probably will not see her invest in B2C, DTC, long-sales-cycle enterprise, bio/medtech, hardware-only, crypto, mobile apps or games. recent_deals is intentionally empty because no reliable public 2024-07-02+ named financing event was found that clearly attributes a priced startup round to CMACK Ventures as the syndicate vehicle. Official portfolio context names Cake Equity, Upflowy, Tiliter and Bridge, but the page does not provide enough dated round evidence or CMACK vehicle attribution to treat them as recent_deals. cheque_ranges is empty because public sources do not disclose founder cheque size, syndicate contribution size or round-size evidence; do not infer cheque size from Aussie Angels membership or Cheryl''s personal angel activity. lead_behavior is participant because the official page says Cheryl will not be the biggest cheque but aims to be the biggest champion. Use for B2B pre-seed/seed founder routing where hands-on GTM, community, startup-network and angel-syndicate access matter; rank below direct VCs and angel groups with verified in-window investment evidence.'
),
