  'Included for ANZ non-dilutive growth funding / debt-provider routing, not VC equity matching: Tractor Ventures provides growth capital, lines of credit and R&D advances for AU/NZ SMEs, software companies, ecommerce brands and VC-backed startups. Official site says businesses can access A$100k-A$3m, has disbursed A$140m+ to 250+ companies, and supports software, ecommerce, B2C apps, marketplaces, services businesses and VC-backed startups. LinkedIn describes Tractor as an alt-capital provider for Australian and New Zealand technology companies, headquartered in Carlton, Victoria and founded in 2020. recent_deals include Aristotle Metadata''s A$400k venture debt and Flowstate''s A$600k debt funding from Tractor Ventures; these are non-dilutive debt/funding events, not equity rounds, and should not be used for VC round-size scoring. Do not use Tractor''s anonymised fresh deals as recent_deals because they lack company names. cheque_ranges are official debt/facility terms, not equity cheque size and not round-size evidence. lead_behavior is unknown to avoid treating debt provision as VC lead or participant behavior; the debt-provider role is captured in investor_type, recent_deals.role and notes. Hard matching gate should be AU/NZ + revenue-generating + non-dilutive capital need + repayment capacity, not broad sector tags. investor_type = debt_provider requires controlled vocabulary support. Use when founder wants non-dilutive capital, R&D advance, inventory/working-capital, runway bridge or growth capital; do not rank as a seed VC lead.'
