  'Watchlist for Queensland non-dilutive grant/support matching, not VC or angel matching: Advance Queensland''s Ignite Ideas Fund supports Queensland SMEs with high-growth potential to commercialise innovative products or services that are at MVP stage or beyond. Official terms provide Tier 1 grants up to A$100k and Tier 2 grants greater than A$100k up to A$200k, with cash-contribution requirements and additional Ignite+ business development support. Applications for Ignite Ideas are currently closed, so use this as a future-round alert/pathway rather than an immediately available funding option. cheque_ranges combine both tiers as official non-dilutive grant terms with no stated floor and a maximum of A$200k; they are not equity cheque sizes. recent_deals are representative 2025 Ignite Ideas grant recipients, not equity rounds and not investor-led financing events; all dates use 2025-01-01 as a year-level approximation because the official recipient page identifies the 2025 round but does not provide individual award dates. lead_behavior is unknown to avoid treating grants as VC lead/participant behavior. Do not use these records for VC round-size or lead-behavior scoring. The hard gate is Queensland-headquartered SME + MVP-or-beyond commercialisation project + grant eligibility, not sector alone. sector_focus is broad because Advance Queensland covers many innovation sectors; AI appetite is medium based on multiple 2025 AI-related recipients and official topic coverage. founder_fit is conservative because female/Indigenous founder support exists elsewhere in the Advance Queensland ecosystem but is not an Ignite Ideas hard mandate. Use this record for grant/support routing and non-dilutive funding options, not investor shortlists.'
),
