  ARRAY['website_form', 'warm_intro'],
  'website_form',
  'included',
  'medium',
  'Included for Victoria-linked deeptech, research-commercialisation and patient-capital matching, not as a generic VC shortlist entry. Breakthrough Victoria was launched in 2021 as a private investment company for Victoria and is now becoming part of Innovation Victoria; LaunchVic''s transition page says Breakthrough Victoria''s investment, follow-on capital, commercialisation and patient-capital activities continue. Official pages say it invests across advanced manufacturing, agri-food, clean economy, digital technologies, and health/life sciences, with typical program ranges of A$150k for research translation/pre-seed, A$1m-A$5m for venture capital and A$10m-A$15m for growth capital. It requires Victoria economic/social/environmental impact and can invest outside Victoria only where there is a clear plan to expand or create benefit in Victoria. recent_deals now capture the main official in-window direct investment updates found on Breakthrough Victoria''s News page, including AlleSense, xCystence Bio, Deftbiotech, Quantum Brilliance, Harvest B, Monash pre-seed/UIP investments, Diag-nose.io, ElectraLith, Type One Energy, Umps Health, Conflux, Viridian, Number 8 Bio, JigSpace and Millibeam. cheque_ranges are official Breakthrough Victoria investment program terms, not inferred round-size evidence. lead_behavior is participant because the FAQ says it expects co-investors, prefers to support other lead investors and generally will not take more than one third of a round; JigSpace is a lead example but should not make this behave like a normal lead VC in matching. Use for Victorian impact, deeptech/research translation, university spinout and growth-capital pathways; rank lower for ordinary SaaS seed founders without a strong Victoria impact or commercialisation link.'
),
