  $json$[{"date":"2025-12-16","company":"Ferronova","company_geography":"australia","direction":"Image-guided cancer surgery tracer and oncology diagnostics technology","business_model":"B2B / medtech / diagnostics","round":"Series A / follow-on","amount_text":"A$6m","amount_value":6000000,"amount_currency":"AUD","role":"Co-lead","investor_evidence_url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/aussie-medtech-ferronova-raises-another-6-million-to-advance-image-guided-cancer-surgery-302643124.html"}]$json$::jsonb,
  ARRAY['website_form', 'email', 'warm_intro'],
  'website_form',
  'included',
  'medium',
  'Included for South Australian government-backed VC / co-investment matching, not generic ANZ VC ranking. SAVCF is a A$50m South Australian Venture Capital Fund established in 2017, backed by SAFA and managed by Artesian Venture Partners. business.gov.au lists the program as Open with applications accepted at any time, and the SAVCF official site provides an apply path and contact email. Official eligibility requires high-growth/export-potential companies with market validation or revenue path, and 50% of assets and staff located in South Australia for 12 months from initial investment. geography_focus is SA-specific, not broader regional Australia. cheque_ranges are official investment terms: seed investments up to A$400k per company and Series A investments of A$2.5m; do not infer cheque fit from historical fund size. recent_deals includes Ferronova''s 2025 A$6m Series A / follow-on round, led by existing investors including SAVCF, Uniseed/UniSuper, Artesian Venture Partners and Renew Pharmaceuticals. lead_behavior is co_lead because SAVCF official terms say it may lead Series A but not always, and Ferronova provides co-lead-style evidence; do not treat it as a generic institutional lead VC for non-SA founders. Use for SA companies in B2B software, space/deeptech, clean energy, cybersecurity, defence, agrifood, health/medtech and related high-growth sectors. AI is not an official SAVCF thesis tag and should only be treated as a weak inference where a specific SA B2B software/deeptech company has AI relevance. Do not rank for non-SA founders or ordinary grant/support matching.'
),
