  'watchlist',
  'medium',
  'Watchlist for Western Australia non-dilutive grant/support matching, not VC or angel matching: the WA Government has invested A$40m into the New Industries and Innovation Fund over 2025-29, replacing the earlier New Industries Fund established in 2017. NIIF funds WA startups, innovation-driven SMEs and ecosystem providers through grants such as the Innovation Booster Grant, Commercialisation Bridge Grant, Innovation Pathways Program and WAVES. Applications for current listed NIIF grants are closed as of the checked pages, with the Innovation Booster Grant page saying the next round is planned for Aug/Sep 2026; use this as a WA grant pathway / future-round alert rather than immediately available capital. cheque_ranges include only direct founder/company grant pathways: IBG up to A$50k and CBG A$50k-A$250k for seed/growth commercialisation support. Do not treat IPP program-provider funding or WAVES venture-fund support as founder cheque evidence. recent_deals are representative 2025 grant recipients, not equity rounds and not investor-led financing events; CBG dates use the official recipient page update date, while IBG dates use 2025-01-01 as year-level approximation because individual award dates are not provided. lead_behavior is unknown to avoid treating grant/support provision as VC lead or participant behavior. stage_focus uses growth only as grant/support lifecycle context, not institutional Series A financing. The hard gate is WA-based startup/SME or WA innovation ecosystem eligibility, not sector alone. Targeted support or favourable assessment exists for regional WA, female-founded and First Nations-founded businesses, but these are not treated as hard founder_fit tags in this MVP record. Use for grant/support routing, non-dilutive funding options and future-round alerts, not capital-first investor shortlists or VC round-size scoring.'
),
