  'website_form',
  'included',
  'medium',
  'Included as a current Canberra/ACT early-stage equity fund, but with limited revealed-deal evidence because ACTivate Capital was publicly announced in November 2025 and no specific ACTivate portfolio-company investment announcements were found in the 2024-07-03 to 2026-07-03 search window. Official website claims pre-seed, seed and Series A investing for founders based in the Canberra region or willing to relocate core business activities; ACT Government''s 2025-11-03 launch release says the ACTivate Capital Fund is live, starts with A$23m committed capital, has capacity to grow to A$50m, and will focus on Canberra-based companies in early growth stages. Startup Daily also reported the A$23m first close toward a A$50m ESVCLP target, with ACT Government as cornerstone investor, Epicorp as general partner, and UNSW Canberra/local family offices as LPs. Do not treat the A$50m fund target or A$23m first close as founder cheque evidence; cheque_ranges are left empty until direct cheque-size terms or actual round participation is disclosed. Sector focus is based on official/government/local-research claims and Startup Daily reporting on defence, quantum, clean energy, advanced manufacturing and AI; the website itself is broader and local-first, so B2B SaaS is not retained as a sector tag. lead_behavior is unknown because no company-level ACTivate rounds have been disclosed. recent_deals is intentionally an empty array rather than omitted: validation searches found no public ACTivate company-level investment/grant/debt/support events, and predecessor Epicorp/ANU Connect historic investments such as Seeing Machines, Instaclustr, Windlab, Cohda Wireless and Mediaware are not attributed as ACTivate recent deals. Use for Canberra-region technical founders, research commercialisation and local relocation-fit companies; recheck before outreach because the fund is new and public portfolio evidence is still sparse.'
),
