  'medium',
  'Federal government non-dilutive grant and advisory program for innovative Australian startups and SMEs commercialising or growing projects in National Reconstruction Fund priority areas. Official business.gov.au page says the program is currently paused to new applications, so use as a watchlist / recheck-before-outreach pathway rather than an immediately open grant. It provides adviser support and, after an Advisory Service report, possible matched grant opportunities: A$50k-A$250k for Early-Stage Commercialisation projects and A$100k-A$5m for Commercialisation and Growth projects. cheque_ranges use only official direct grant terms, not the total program pool. recent_deals are representative official grant recipients from the business.gov.au recipient list; they are grant awards and not VC equity rounds. Recipient list currently reports 140 grants totalling A$209.5m excluding GST, but individual award dates are not published on the recipient page, so recent_deals use the 2026-07-03 verification date and source-notes flag the date limitation. lead_behavior is unknown to keep VC lead/co-lead/participant scoring clean; grant-provider meaning is captured in recent_deals.role and notes only. Strong fit for Australian manufacturing capability, deeptech, medtech, defence, renewables/low-emissions, resources, transport, agtech and enabling-capability startups; weak fit for ordinary SaaS, consumer apps, marketplaces or founders outside NRF priority areas.'
),
